column47:
Create a new procedure"{*}MDM_AGREEMENT_SO{*}" in "{*}PAYMENTS_AGREEMENTS_MDM.MDM_PAYLOAD_MESSAGE_GENERATION{*}" (PAYRUN-1515) to generate payload message for Standing Order product in CORE DBs (LT, EE, LV) 

The new procedure must be able to:
 * Generate [Agreement Summary payloads|https://wiki.swedbank.net/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=842727454#expand-Engagementpayload] messages based on input parameters and add it into queue "{*}PAYMENTS_AGREEMENTS_MDM.MDM_MESSAGES{*}" (PAYRUN-1390)

Input parameters:
 * i_operation - VARCHAR2, possible values: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE;
 * i_agreement_id - NUMBER, crebit.per_mk.pmk_nr
 * i_status - VARCHAR2, crebit.per_mk.staatus
 * i_dt_from - DATE, crebit.per_mk.keht_akp
 * i_dt_till - DATE, crebit.per_mk.annul_kp or crebit.keht_lkp or NULL;  (to understand read pinned comment)
 * i_last_updated_time - TIMESTAMP, cast crebit.per_mk.changed_date to timestamp
 * i_account_id - VARCHAR2, crebit.per_mk.anr
 * i_customer_id - VARCHAR2, for message generation on account change event

On input parameter *i_operation* value *INSERT* or *UPDATE* generate the following payload message:
{code:java}
{
  "sourceSystemId": "",         // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "PAYMENTS" as value 
  "correlationId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_CREBIT.PER_MK[PMK_NR]", Format:20240509_110414_6940174571   
  "instanceId": "",             // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string)- use "EE", "LT", "LV" as value based on engagement origin country context
  "type": "",                   // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ENGAGEMENT" as value
  "lastModifiedTimestamp": ,    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use CREBIT.PER_MK CHANGED_DATE table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
  "operation": "",              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) depends on type of event trigger captured, possible values: "INSERT", "UPDATE"
  "payload": {                  // (object) Details of the change
    "engagementSourceRef": "",  // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "CREBIT.PER_MK[PMK_NR]",  Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>]         
    "type": "",                 // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "STANDING_ORDER_AGREEMENT" as value
    "status": "",               // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use CREBIT.PER_MK STAATUS table column value
    "nr": "",                   // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use CREBIT.PER_MK PMK_NR table column value      
    "startDate": ,              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use CREBIT.PER_MK KEHT_AKP, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
    "endDate": ,                // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use CREBIT.KEHT_LKP (date set by client when his agreement ends) or CREBIT.PER_MK ANNUL_KP (manual cancellation of ongoing agreement) or can be NULL (until manual cancellation), format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
    "partyRoles": [             // (list) List of all party roles related to this engagement
      {
        "roleSourceRef": "",    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use CREBIT.PER_MK[PMK_NR] Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>].
        "partyId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) NULL
        "role": "",             // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "STANDING_ORDER_PAYER" as value
        "startDate": ,          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use CREBIT.PER_MK KEHT_AKP table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
        "endDate":              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use CREBIT.PER_MK ANNUL_KP table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
     }
    ]
  }
}{code}
On input parameter *i_operation* value *DELETE* generate the following payload message: 
{code:java}
{
  "sourceSystemId": "",         // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "PAYMENTS" as value 
  "correlationId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_CREBIT.PER_MK[PMK_NR]", Format:20240509_110414_6940174571   
  "instanceId": "",             // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string)- use "EE", "LT", "LV" as value based on engagement origin country context
  "type": "",                   // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ENGAGEMENT" as value
  "lastModifiedTimestamp": ,    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use (TBD), format: unix timestamp milliseconds
  "operation": "",              // STATIC VALUE - (string) possible value: "DELETE"
  "payload": {                  // (object) Details of the change
    "engagementSourceRef": ""  // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "CREBIT.PER_MK[PMK_NR]",  Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>]         
  }
}{code}
{color:#de350b}In case i_customer_id is empty, add i_account_id value into USER_DATA.HEADER.PROPERTIES collection:
"account_no": "", // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use CREBIT.PER_MK ANR (this field and value are temporary as been used only for data {color}
----
 

*Examples* from other product areas

