column47:
*Why:* not valid payment file will fail in later stages.
*When:* 
*Where:* worker-payment-batch-handler
*What:*

Update payment file validation:
 # If payment file contains mass payment, validate that number_of_transactions on header level and on payment information level is the same and matches transactions in the file (ERR00002)
 # If payment file contains mass payment, validate that control_sum on header level and on payment information level is the same and matches transactions in the file (ERR00003)
 # Validate Payment_type_information is present either on Payment information level, or on Credit transaction level for each Credit transaction (ERR00011)
 # Validate that Payment type information → Category purpose → Code contains only SALA. If any other value is provided - ignore it as if not provided.

 

Update this part of validation (new part in orange):

Precondition: tag <CstmrCdtTrfInitn><PmtInf><PmtTpInf><CtgyPurp><Cd> contains 'SALA'
 # Check that first two symbols of each creditor account (CstmrCdtTrfInitn><PmtInf><CdtTrfTxInf><CdtrAcct>) matches the first two symbols of debtor account (CstmrCdtTrfInitn><PmtInf><DbtrAcct>) and matches debtor country code (that is: all payments are domestic)
 # Check that currency (CstmrCdtTrfInitn><PmtInf><CdtTrfTxInf><InstdAmt Ccy="EUR">) is EUR for all transactions
 ## {color:#ff8b00}If it's not EUR, then:{color}
 ### {color:#ff8b00}Check that currency is the same for all payments{color}
 ### {color:#ff8b00}Check that account number is intrabank, that is:{color}
 #### {color:#ff8b00}For LT: 5-9 symbols are: 73000{color}
 #### {color:#ff8b00}For LV: 5-8 symbols are: HABA{color}
 #### {color:#ff8b00}For EE: 5-6 symbols are: 22{color}
 # If both validations are successful - proceed with updating file status to Validated. If not - reject file with error - see the table at the bottom

*Why:* 

1. According to [Instant Payments Regulation|https://www.ecb.europa.eu/paym/integration/retail/instant_payments/html/instant_payments_regulation.en.html] and [2025 EPC Payment Scheme Rulebooks|https://www.europeanpaymentscouncil.eu/news-insights/news/revised-entry-force-dates-2025-epc-payment-scheme-rulebooks-and-version-10-epc], payment service providers (PSPs) must to offer for all private and corporate customers (payment service users - PSU) two new payment limits: 
 * Instant payment daily limit.
 * Instant payment transaction limit.

*When:* On agreed date after organizing communication to customers; at latest {color:#172b4d}5{color} of October 2025.
*Where:*

In iBank Private and Business -> Daily banking -> New payment -> tab: "Domestic or European", SMART payment form

Note: Although it is possible to initiate SEPA payments and Swedbank group payments in EUR via tab "International", from there initiated payment will be processed as regular/ urgent via STEP2 system, i.e. no possibility to initiate instant payment from this tab, therefore no need to implement changes described below in this tab. 

*What:* 

*{color:#172b4d}Possible use cases (see detailed description in wiki page UC1 -UC3 [Use cases - customer has disabled instant payments/ exceeded IP limits - Payments Baltics VDE - Swedbank IT Wiki|https://wiki.swedbank.net/spaces/DPAY/pages/2419818556/Use+cases+-+customer+has+disabled+instant+payments+exceeded+IP+limits]):{color}*

*{color:#172b4d}UC1.{color}* Customer has disabled instant payments (IP);

*UC2:*
 * Initiated payment amount exceeds daily IP limit;
 * Permanent daily payment Teleagreement limit is NOT exceeded; 
 * Permanent monthly payment Teleagreement limit is NOT exceeded.

*UC3:*
 * Initiated payment amount exceeds transaction IP limit;
 * Permanent daily payment Teleagreement limit is NOT exceeded;  
 * Permanent monthly payment Teleagreement limit is NOT exceeded.

*{color:#172b4d}Pre-condition:{color}*
 * {color:#172b4d}For Beneficiary's account entered by customer SEPA domestic and cross-border instant payments are enabled. {color}

{color:#172b4d}1. After customer enters amount in SMART payment form, then:{color}

{color:#172b4d}1) It should be automatically hidden value "Instant" in field Payment priority AND {color}{color:#172b4d}showed two options: {color}
 * {color:#172b4d}EE, LT: "Ordinary"/LV: "Economy" and {color}
 * {color:#172b4d}PB: "Urgent"/ "Express"{color}{color:#172b4d}; {color}

{color:#172b4d}3) By default it should be checked Payment priority: EE, LT: "Ordinary"/LV: "Economy";{color}

{color:#172b4d}4) According to customer choice it must be allowed to initiate payment with payment type "Normal" or "Urgent" (?) {color}(CREBIT.DP.DOC_PRIORITY='N' OR 'U' (?)).

!image-2025-06-26-11-58-31-260.png|width=819,height=652!

The same automated payment type switch and UI requirements are applicable in case customer is initiating payment from:
 # New payment: iBank Private and Business -> Daily banking -> New payment -> tab: "Domestic or European", SMART payment form;
 # From defined payments;
 # From account statements
 # Manual payment from received E-invoice;
 # LV Bank defined payments when payment is opened in SMART payment form;
 # Payment initiated from Group Account member account.

(!){*}Note{*}: Exception for payments opened from *List of Payments.* For payment opened from List of payments it is applied different logic. More details see SMARTPAY-750 iBank: Private and Business PB: Re-factor display of payment types when user navigating from the List Of Payment to The Smart Form - Swedbank:
 * 
 ** There are showed 3 payment priorities: "Instant", "Ordinary", "Urgent". 
 ** No automated payment type switch in such cases:
 *** Payment in SMART payment form where amount was not exceeding IP limit was saved to List of payments, then payment is opened again from List of payments, previously added amount is deleted and again entered other amount which is exceeding IP limit: payment priority is showed "Instant"; customer can choose other payment type: “Instant” or “Ordinary”. 
 *** Payment in SMART payment form where amount was exceeding IP limit, then it is opened payment from List of payments, automatically it is showed as “Ordinary” payment type; Customer can choose other payment type: “Instant” or “Regular”.

 

