column637:
17.12.2024 08:22;p998osm;For QA:

1. Add to the queue not existing crebit.dp id's

begin
  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.put_message(1);
  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.put_message(2);
  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.put_message(3);
  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.put_message(4);
  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.put_message(5);

  commit;
end;


2. After 5 non-successful tries to dequeue messages (each try after 30 sec), messages will be put into dead letter queue:

select * from payments.aq$q_dp_for_kafka_msg;

!image-2024-12-17-09-15-07-991.png|width=683,height=110!

3. Run restoring procedures:

payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.restore_all_messages
payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.restore_message(i_msgid IN VARCHAR2)

For example:

BEGIN

  payments.dp_for_kafka_q_api.restore_all_messages;

  commit;

END;

4. Check if messages are returned to normal queue (but do it as soon as it possible, as after 5 non successful retries they'll will be putted back to dead letter queue).  Msg_id will be changed to new!!!

select * from payments.aq$q_dp_for_kafka_msg;

!image-2024-12-17-09-21-00-101.png|width=820,height=153!

 

 ;;;

