column637:
03.09.2024 10:13;p998gkm;Tested in PPTE.

Testing was done by performing einvoince performance regression part as well as processing standing orders (with the new sysglobal enabled):

BEGIN
  crebit.per_mk_tootl.registreeri_maksmisele;
  crebit.per_mk_tootl.maksa_summata;
  crebit.per_mk_tootl.maksa_summaga;
END;

It was then possible to find standing orders and einvoices here:

 select * from crebit.dp where in_channel_code in ('SOP','PKM') and status in ('C','N','R') order by 1 desc 

And importing crebit.dp ID values into the select Olga provided to see if these payments also appeared in the Kafka queue:

SELECT l.user_data.header.get_long_property('id'), l.*
  FROM payments.aq$q_dp_for_kafka_msg l
 WHERE l.user_data.header.get_long_property('id') IN (list of crebit.dp.id values);;;

