column644:
17.01.2024 14:17;p998gkm;Tested in PPTE.

Common observations: when the payment is being processed in SEPA Exchange, API calls to MDM are performed:

Making a request to MDM API: Request\{method=GET, url=https://mdm-test.sbcore.net/lv/v2/parties/B0000002/addresses?type=CONTACT_ADDRESS, tags={}}
Received a response from MDM API: Response\{protocol=http/1.1, code=200, message=OK, url=https://mdm-test.sbcore.net/lv/v2/parties/B0000002/addresses?type=CONTACT_ADDRESS}

When testing in LTU: I've managed to find and test with users who only have one address available, for example: only contact address or residence address. In case there's only a residence address available, when MDM call is performed - Contact Address is being asked for, if that data comes back empty, another call is performed that looks for residence address. 

In LV and EE I was unsuccessful to test these scenarios, it appears we no can longer remove addresses from DB as there are triggers in place. But Contact Address is successfully fetched and filled in  payments.iso_post_address table. 

 

Tested with a EUR payment to a non EU/EAA country.;;;

