column637:
30.11.2023 08:35;annyk;Additional business requirement: *Intragroup incoming payments must not be screened* as they already are screened on outgoing side. 

_29.11.2023: "Based on discussion with local teams and also within BB AFC it is our understanding that *as-is business logic* (submitting payment for ProScan {*}screening only for outgoing part/leg{*}) for processing *intra-group payments* shall remain the same after SEPA flows are merged. We assume it was well weighted risk based approach when implemented which also allows for additional efficiency in payment screening process. Changing it now without proper assessment which is backed by statistics and other relevant metrics would not be correct. We will keep looking into this rule also next year as several efficiency items were brought to our table in connection to potential update of EU regulation related to instant schema and other relevant cases."_

 

Based on the comment it is likely that this rule will change in future. Proposal from Mykolas is to *introduce screening rule table* similar to one for ISOExchange as we already have many different business requirements regarding screening.;;;

