column47:
* Validate incoming cross-border SEPA payment {-}as it is now in FP{-};
 * Save cross-border SEPA payment data into a single data store;

 

*Acceptance criteria:*

1. Incoming payment is saved in DP with following out_channel_code:
 * Domestic payment /return (BIC country is local country) - 'SEPI' (as is)
 * Cross-border payment/return (BIC country is not local country {-}and BIC is not intragroup BIC{-})- 'SEPCI'
 * _-Intragroup payment/return (BIC is intragroup BIC (HG_SWIFT_LIST))- 'SEPGI' – this task or- with PAYRUN-10?_

2. Creditor reference validation is not done for cross-border and intragroup payment; is still done for domestic (See DPAY-2056 for rules)

3.{color:#172b4d} Check also service_limitation -> we should check cross-border and intragroup with 'FPI', not 'LPC'{color}

{color:#172b4d}4. Any other validations are same as for incoming domestic payments.{color}

