column47:
Create a new procedure"{*}MDM_AGREEMENT_ALIAS{*}" in "{*}PAYMENTS_AGREEMENTS_MDM.MDM_PAYLOAD_MESSAGE_GENERATION{*}" (PAYRUN-1515) to generate payload message for Account alias product in CORE DBs (LT, EE, LV) 

The new procedure must be able to:
 * Generate [Agreement Summary payloads|https://wiki.swedbank.net/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=842727454#expand-Engagementpayload] messages based on input parameters and add it into queue "{*}PAYMENTS_AGREEMENTS_MDM.MDM_MESSAGES{*}" (PAYRUN-1390)

Input parameters:
 * i_operation - VARCHAR2, possible values: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE;
 * i_agreement_id - NUMBER, account_alias.alias.id
 * i_status - VARCHAR2, account_alias.alias.status
 * i_dt_from - DATE, account_alias.alias.valid_from
 * i_dt_till - DATE, account_alias.alias.valid_until
 * i_last_updated_time - TIMESTAMP, cast account_alias.alias.last_modified_at to timestamp
 * i_customer_id - VARCHAR2, account_alias.alias.customer_id

On input parameter *i_operation* value *INSERT* or *UPDATE* generate the following payload message:
{code:java}
{
  "sourceSystemId": "",         // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "PAYMENTS" as value 
  "correlationId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_ACCOUNT_ALIAS.ALIAS[ID]", Format:20240509_110414_6940174571   
  "instanceId": "",             // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string)- use "EE", "LT", "LV" as value based on engagement origin country context
  "type": "",                   // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ENGAGEMENT" as value
  "lastModifiedTimestamp": ,    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS LAST_MODIFIED_AT table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
  "operation": "",              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) depends on type of event trigger captured, possible values: "INSERT", "UPDATE"
  "payload": {                  // (object) Details of the change
    "engagementSourceRef": "",  // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "ACCOUNT_ALIAS[ID]",  Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>]         
    "type": "",                 // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ACCOUNT_ALIAS_AGREEMENT" as value
    "status": "",               // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS STATUS table column value
    "nr": "",                   // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS ID table column value      
    "startDate": ,              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS VALID_FROM, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
    "endDate": ,                // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS VALID_UNTIL, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
    "partyRoles": [             // (list) List of all party roles related to this engagement
      {
        "roleSourceRef": "",    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS[ID] Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>].
        "partyId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS CUSTOMER_ID
        "role": "",             // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ACCOUNT_ALIAS_BENEFICIARY" as value
        "startDate": ,          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS VALID_FROM table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
        "endDate":              // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use ACCOUNT_ALIAS VALID_UNTIL table column value, format: unix timestamp milliseconds, sys_extract_utc
     }
    ]
  }
}{code}
On input parameter *i_operation* value *DELETE* generate the following payload message: 
{code:java}
{
  "sourceSystemId": "",         // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "PAYMENTS" as value 
  "correlationId": "",          // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_ACCOUNT_ALIAS[ID]", Format:20240509_110414_6940174571   
  "instanceId": "",             // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string)- use "EE", "LT", "LV" as value based on engagement origin country context
  "type": "",                   // STATIC VALUE - (string) - use "ENGAGEMENT" as value
  "lastModifiedTimestamp": ,    // DYNAMIC VALUE - (long timestamp) - use (TBD), format: unix timestamp milliseconds
  "operation": "",              // STATIC VALUE - (string) possible value: "DELETE"
  "payload": {                  // (object) Details of the change
    "engagementSourceRef": ""  // DYNAMIC VALUE - (string) - use "ACCOUNT_ALIAS[ID]",  Format: <shema_name>.<table_name>[<unique record_id>]         
  }
}{code}
----
 

*Examples* from other product areas

*UPDATE* operation (ENGAGEMENT payload example from Leasing):
