column47:
*Issue:* Error in Batch Handler when Debtor name is not filled in pain.001 file. According MIG Debtor name is not mandatory to have in file as we anyway replace it with name from our database.

*Steps to reproduce:*

Import file with empty Debtor element:

<Dbtr/>

*Expected results:*
Payment is processed and sent for FM

*Actual results:* 
Error in logs, payment not processed

 

*Additional information:* 

1. Update validation in API [payment/create:|https://core-payment-batch-handler-data-manager-dev.apps.scp-west-zone01-z02.swedbank.io/swagger-ui/index.html#/Payment%20batch%20handler%20data%20manager%20payment/createPayment]

{color:#172b4d}Allow not to provide Debtor name. Previous validation: these fields can only be all provided together - if at least one is missing, there should be error in API response. If all are missing - do not create entry in payment_info table{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}Instructed amount - optional{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}Currency - optional{color}
 * -{color:#ffab00}Debtor name - optional{color}-
 * {color:#172b4d}Debtor account number - optional{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}Creditor name - optional{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}Creditor account number - optional{color}
 * {color:#172b4d}Creditor account type - optional{color}

2. Update Kafka schema for topic payment.orders - field debtor name has to be made as optional:

!image-2026-02-05-10-29-35-865.png!

Full schema: [https://myntet.sharepoint.com/:x:/r/teams/PaymentsBaltic/_layouts/15/Doc.aspx?sourcedoc=%7B40D07A2A-3F8A-411A-A225-7BC4B3186EB9%7D&file=Payment_order_data.xlsx&action=default&mobileredirect=true]

