column636:
17.06.2024 08:58;p998udz;During archiving process trying to delete data from vm.sepa_document table, but table vm.sepa_system_event_note has a records with FK to vm.sepa_document, FK violation error appears.

 

Table vm.sepa_system_event_note was introduced with sepa rulebook 2023 start. Sepa rulebook started at the same time in all 3 countries 90 days before, sepa_documents archiving archives 90+ days old data, that's why error appeared at the same time in all 3 countries.

 

Solution: include table vm.sepa_system_event_note into archiving process or remove FK to v.sepa_document;;;

20.06.2024 08:13;rasart; {{CREBIT.DP.UNSTRUCTURED_REMITTANCE_INFO}} is filled:

!image-2024-06-20-09-13-12-646.png!

 ;;;

column47:
Include in archiving process (VM.FP_ARCHIVE.move_sepa_msg_to_arch) archiving of document_type SYS_E_NOTE and records of {{VM.SEPA_SYSTEM_EVENT_NOTE}} table.

For that purpose:
 * create table {{VM.SEPA_SYSTEM_EVENT_NOTE_ARCH in Core}}
 * {{add archiving of document_type SYS_E_NOTE (currently it is excluded - EASYPAY-580) and VM.SEPA_SYSTEM_EVENT_NOTE table to VM.FP_ARCHIVE.move_sepa_msg_to_arch (Core DB)}}

Setup similar to others vm.sepa_....arch tables.

As this table is growing very slowly (less that 200 records per month), let's keep it only in Core DB, no need to move records to Arch DB.

