27.11.2025 12:36;matve;I will discuss this with [~p998hdf] upon her return as the feature was not pulled in, but I will state my suggestion here:

There could be a case, that when fraud-screening request is sent, then the application crashes before managing to update the fraud-screening record in Batch Handler's database with status, transaction id and sent time - I would suggest to save that data while the response readiness message is received from Kafka and fraud-screening record is updated to status "In processing".

Then the value of "transactionId" should be passed to update API and due to the endpoint's validation rules also a value for "request_sent_dtime" should be passed (can we leave it not saved as it would be a fake value?). And perhaps also the update of "response_received_dtime" could be done here (updated also during fraud-screening completion, same value?), then it can be used to skip the "response_timeout_dtime" calculation step when response has already been received. It also affects the endpoint action to end with failure if already existing "transaction_id" value is attempted to overwrite - it could check, that if the value is to be updated to the same value, then failure is not raised and update continues.;;;

