column47:
This sub-task for error codes which should be updated/changed

 
 # *ERR00004* *Mass payment contains international payments* -  we do not receive this error code when mass payment contains international payments, now we get *ERR00005 - General error - if no other error found.*

*{color:#172b4d}Need to change from ERR00005 to ERR00004 for Mass payments{color}*

 

          {*}{color:#172b4d}2{color}{color:#172b4d}*.* ERR00002{color}{*}{color:#172b4d}(Number of transactions in the file does not match with transactions count in the file){color} ** {color:#172b4d}is shown when mass payment file  has more than one  PmtInf block. Is it ok - need to discuss?{color}{*}{{*}}

{color:#172b4d}          *3.* *ERR00005* (General error - if no other error found) is shown when mass payments file  has payments in non-EUR currencies to other banks.{color}

{color:#172b4d}         {*}4. If mass payment has >1 PmtInf blocks -  file is rejected with ERR00004{*}(Mass payment contains international payments). This error code is not OK for this issue. Maybe another, more informative code could be created? Use error code ERR00011{color}

Issue reproduced with pain.001.001.009 by providing not existing debtors account:
!image-2025-12-30-16-03-24-713.png|thumbnail! 
payment file was validated in DB:
!image-2025-12-30-16-04-28-683.png|thumbnail! 
*Batch was not rejected with error code ERR00008 - NOK*
!image-2025-12-30-16-05-28-109.png|thumbnail!

 

*AS IS* - error is thrown in logs that account was not found (accounts API response is such)

*TO BE* - batch status should be changed to rejected with error code ERR00008, pain.002 should be created for the batch

 

WARNS and Errors in logs:
