column636:
13.02.2026 11:38;andmku;Following applications has been upgraded to the latest compatible components/dependencies, including Spring Framework ({*}6.2.15{*}):
 * {{payment-services-discovery}}
 * {{payment-archive-service}}
 * {{payment-service}}
 * {{payment-form-service}}
 * {{payment-services-gateway}}

Fix has been verified via vulnerability scanner: [https://twistlock-console.apps.scp-west-zone02-p01.swedbank.net|https://twistlock-console.apps.scp-west-zone02-p01.swedbank.net/]

 

{color:#de350b}*No upgrade for {{{}payment-services{}}}.*{color} {{payment-services}} depends on {color:#de350b}*{{bank-components}}*{color}, which depends on very old Spring Framework version, so {color:#de350b}*upgrade is not an option*{color}.

Removal of a vulnerable component ({{{}spring-webmvc{}}}) is also not possible as it's used for application health check HTTP endpoint.

*CVE-2024-38819* impact on {{payment-services}} was checked. It was determined that {{payment-services}} can't be exploited due to these facts:
 * The web application {color:#de350b}*is not*{color} using {{RouterFunctions}} to serve static resources.
 * Resource handling {color:#de350b}*is not*{color} explicitly configured with a FileSystemResource location.
 * Web application access is restricted to allow access for health check endpoint only.;;;

